# Matchbox SPLiT-seq -- symmetric quant output (UMI 10 + bc3 8 + bc2 8 + bc1 8, OBSERVED).
# Recovery = linker structure (linkers within ~3 edits, indels allowed); barcodes captured positionally as OBSERVED
# bytes, matching seqproc/splitcode so STARsolo does all barcode correction. bc1 is the 8bp after
# linker2 (captured as `rest`; the stitcher takes rest[:8], since matchbox `_` needs >=1 char and
# the read often ends exactly at bc1). Emits TSV (id, umi, bc3, bc2, rest) -> stitched to cDNA.
linker1 = GTGGCCGCTGTTTCGCATCGGCGTACGACT
linker2 = ATCCACGTGCTTGAGAGGCCAGAGCATTCG

if read matches [umi:|10| bc3:|8| linker1~0.1 bc2:|8| linker2~0.1 rest:_] => {
    '{read.id}\t{umi.seq}\t{bc3.seq}\t{bc2.seq}\t{rest.seq}'.stdout!()
}
